{"page_id": "olmo_old_scans_math-4_pg512-p1", "markdown": "496\n\n# ADVANCED ALGEBRA\n\nEXERCISE 172\n\nSolve by Cardan's method:\n\n1．が3-32-2=0.\n\n2.@-98+28=0.\n\n3．@-182-35=0.\n\n4．2-368-91=0.\n\n5.@ー32+2=0.\n\n6.@2-272-54=0.\n\n7. 2+92+26=0.\n\n8.@3-722-280=0.\n\n9. 2-6+9=0.\n\n10.@+92-26=0.\n\n11.28-9.-28=0.\n\n12.@-72.+280=0.\n\n13.@-62-12a+112=0.\n\n14、び+52+8.+6=0.\n\nSOLUTION OF BIQUADRATICS\n\n- A biquadratic is an equation of the fourth degree.\n- Descartes' solution of the biquadratic.\n\nLet で+po+@2+1=0.\n\nAssume a+po'+g+r=（2+1+m）（2-12-+n）\n\n＝ゼ+（ーで十m+n）2ー1（m-n）2+mn.\n\nEquating the coefficients, we have\n\nーで+m+n=p，-1（m-n）=9,mn=r.\n\n(3)\n\nConsidering that (m + n) - (m - n)?- 4 mn =0, it is easy to eliminate m and n. We obtain\n\nで＋2pで+（パー4ヶ）8-9=0.\n\n(4)\n\nEquation (4) is a cubic in P, which has always one real\n\npositive root.\n\nWhen I is known, the values of m and n are\n\ndetermined from equation (3). The solutions of the two equations\n\n2十1+m=0\n\nand\n\n2ー1+n=0\n\nproduce the required roots.", "width": 902, "height": 1434, "blocks": [{"kind": "text", "text": "496", "bbox": {"x": 101.54966873479027, "y": 104.56249992033328, "width": 47.78807947019867, "height": 23.900000000000073}}, {"kind": "heading", "text": "ADVANCED ALGEBRA", "bbox": {"x": 328.54304614932903, "y": 107.54999997248358, "width": 289.7152317880795, "height": 20.912499999999927}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "EXERCISE 172", "bbox": {"x": 388.27814644205296, "y": 173.27499986929683, "width": 173.2317880794702, "height": 20.912500000000087}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Solve by Cardan's method:", "bbox": {"x": 131.41721838631565, "y": 221.0749999852104, "width": 322.56953642384116, "height": 29.875000000000053}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "1．が3-32-2=0.", "bbox": {"x": 131.4172170123345, "y": 262.89999970125, "width": 224.00662251655632, "height": 23.900000000000073}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "2.@-98+28=0.", "bbox": {"x": 131.41721839181827, "y": 307.71249998676427, "width": 238.9403